# We formalize x[i] as the number of operations used on edge (i, i+1) mod n, and r[i] as the residual coins at vertex i at termination.
# Constraints per vertex i: x[i-1] + x[i] + r[i] = a[i], with indices mod n.
# Operation count equals sum_i x[i]. Terminal condition: for all i, not (r[i] > 0 and r[i+1] > 0).
# N_max: maximize sum x[i] subject to constraints and nonnegativity. This is attained by choosing r[i] = 0 whenever feasible, i.e., saturating vertices: x[i-1] + x[i] = a[i]. We must also ensure x[i] >= 0.
# N_min: minimize sum x[i], equivalently maximize sum r[i], under the independence constraint and feasibility of the linear system.

# Helper: compute N_max via constructive recurrence with r[i] = 0.
